

> Family are those for whom you lie.  
> Friends are those with whom you lie.  
> Acquaintances are those about whom you lie.  
> Strangers are those to whom you lie.  

---

> Friends can be family, and also acquaintances.  
> Family can be acquaintances, but to be all three is a great risk.  
> When family becomes a stranger, so too does the very identity of the self.  

---

**Awareness is not Optional.**

